{"id":1102998,"xmlId":"NodeJS","name":"Node.js","description":"Provides <a href=\"https://nodejs.org/\">Node.js</a> support to all JetBrains IDEs that\n   <a href=\"https://www.jetbrains.com/products/#lang=js&amp;type=ide\">support JavaScript</a>.\n\n  <h3>Features</h3>\n  <ul>\n  <li>Node.js debugging attachable to a running process</li>\n  <li>Node.js profiler</li>\n  <li>Mocha test debugging and running inside the IDE</li>\n  <li>New Express projects from the Welcome screen</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h3>Getting started</h3>\n  For information on getting started, head over to the <a href=\"https://www.jetbrains.com/help/\">documentation</a> for your IDE.\n  For WebStorm, you can check out this section in the <a href=\"https://www.jetbrains.com/help/webstorm/developing-node-js-applications.html\">documentation</a>.\n\n  <h3>Notes</h3>\n  You can also run and debug Node.js applications in remote environments such as Docker containers, Vagrant machines,\n  and remote servers right from the IDE. For that, please install the\n  <a href=\"https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/8116-node-js-remote-interpreter\">Node.js Remote Interpreter</a> plugin.","organization":"JetBrains s.r.o.","tags":["JavaScript"],"version":"262.8665.177","dependencies":["intellij.json","intellij.javascript.analysis.impl","intellij.javascript.testing","JavaScriptDebugger","intellij.javascript.common","intellij.javascript.backend.scriptDebugger","intellij.platform.coverage","com.intellij.modules.lang","intellij.platform.smRunner","intellij.javascript.psi.impl","intellij.json.backend","com.intellij.modules.scriptDebugger.backend","intellij.javascript.parser","intellij.javascript.backend","JavaScript","com.intellij.modules.ultimate","intellij.platform.testRunner"],"optionalDependencies":["com.intellij.modules.coverage"],"since":"262.8665","until":"262.*","size":976347,"vendor":"JetBrains","depends":["JavaScript","JavaScriptDebugger","com.intellij.modules.lang","com.intellij.modules.ultimate","com.intellij.mo